1
00:00:01,000 --> 00:00:04,478
By default, every tenant is offered the same features.

2
00:00:04,478 --> 00:00:09,985
Tenant feature profiles let the Default tenant decide which features a tenant is offered.

3
00:00:09,985 --> 00:00:14,970
In this video, we create a profile, assign it to a tenant, and check the result.

4
00:00:19,570 --> 00:00:24,144
Without a profile, the Features page of every tenant lists the same features,

5
00:00:24,144 --> 00:00:27,174
apart from those reserved for the Default tenant.

6
00:00:27,174 --> 00:00:32,960
The administrator of a tenant can enable these features, including ones you would rather not offer.

7
00:00:33,710 --> 00:00:38,276
A feature profile is a named list of rules, created on the Default tenant.

8
00:00:38,276 --> 00:00:42,615
When you assign a profile to a tenant, its rules decide which features

9
00:00:42,615 --> 00:00:44,270
that tenant is offered.

10
00:00:45,020 --> 00:00:50,907
Several tenants can share one profile, and a tenant without a profile is not restricted.

11
00:00:50,907 --> 00:00:53,850
Only the Default tenant manages profiles.

12
00:00:58,050 --> 00:01:03,076
Each rule has a Rule, which is Exclude or Include, and an Expression.

13
00:01:03,076 --> 00:01:09,710
The Expression is matched against feature IDs, and it can use wildcards, such as an asterisk.

14
00:01:10,460 --> 00:01:15,720
Rules apply in the order listed, and the last rule that matches a feature decides.

15
00:01:15,720 --> 00:01:20,621
Here, the Include rule brings the SMTP Email Provider back after the Exclude

16
00:01:20,621 --> 00:01:23,012
rule removed every Email provider.

17
00:01:23,012 --> 00:01:26,180
A feature that no rule matches stays available.

18
00:01:26,930 --> 00:01:31,745
A feature is also unavailable when a feature it depends on is excluded.

19
00:01:31,745 --> 00:01:40,250
Excluding Workflows therefore removes HTTP Workflows Activities, Timer Workflows Activities, and Session Workflows Activities too.

20
00:01:44,456 --> 00:01:48,590
Feature profiles belong to the Default tenant, so we start there.

21
00:01:48,590 --> 00:01:52,666
Under Tools, Features, let's search for Tenant Feature Profiles.

22
00:01:53,141 --> 00:01:58,090
Each row shows the name of a feature and, beside it, the feature ID.

23
00:01:58,090 --> 00:02:01,301
The rules of a profile refer to these IDs.

24
00:02:01,761 --> 00:02:02,981
Select Enable.

25
00:02:02,981 --> 00:02:07,619
A notice confirms it, and Multi-Tenancy gets a Feature Profiles entry.

26
00:02:07,619 --> 00:02:13,111
The Administrator role has the Manage tenant feature profiles permission by default.

27
00:02:17,384 --> 00:02:20,505
Open Multi-Tenancy, then Feature Profiles.

28
00:02:20,505 --> 00:02:23,822
The list is empty, because no profile exists.

29
00:02:23,822 --> 00:02:27,204
Select Add Feature Profile to start a new one.

30
00:02:27,662 --> 00:02:31,452
Name is how the profile appears in the list, on the Tenants page,

31
00:02:31,452 --> 00:02:34,174
and in the Feature profile field of a tenant.

32
00:02:34,174 --> 00:02:35,722
We call it Basic sites.

33
00:02:36,188 --> 00:02:38,993
Rules is an editor for the list of rules.

34
00:02:38,993 --> 00:02:43,768
The hint below it shows an example, an Exclude rule for OrchardCore.Flows.

35
00:02:44,220 --> 00:02:45,797
We add three rules.

36
00:02:45,797 --> 00:02:48,762
The first excludes the Workflows feature.

37
00:02:48,762 --> 00:02:53,810
The second uses an asterisk to exclude every Email provider, and the third

38
00:02:53,810 --> 00:02:56,650
includes the SMTP Email Provider again.

39
00:02:57,108 --> 00:02:58,187
Select Save.

40
00:02:58,187 --> 00:03:02,263
The profile appears in the list, with Edit and Delete buttons.

41
00:03:02,263 --> 00:03:06,038
As the list grows, the Search box finds profiles by name.

42
00:03:06,496 --> 00:03:09,238
To change a profile later, select Edit.

43
00:03:09,238 --> 00:03:14,296
The form is the same, with the current rules, and Cancel returns to the list.

44
00:03:18,489 --> 00:03:23,555
The Tenants page lists every tenant, and a separate video covers creating them.

45
00:03:23,555 --> 00:03:27,369
Let's select Edit on Bluebird, a tenant without a profile.

46
00:03:27,872 --> 00:03:33,018
The Feature profile field appears when at least one profile exists, and the

47
00:03:33,018 --> 00:03:35,495
Create Tenant page offers it too.

48
00:03:35,495 --> 00:03:37,782
Select Basic sites, then Save.

49
00:03:38,276 --> 00:03:43,601
Back on the Tenants page, a badge with the profile name marks the row of Bluebird.

50
00:03:43,601 --> 00:03:47,896
Maplewood has no profile badge, because no profile applies to it.

51
00:03:52,108 --> 00:03:54,320
Let's compare the Features pages.

52
00:03:54,320 --> 00:03:59,766
On the Default tenant, a search for OrchardCore.Workflows lists Workflows and the features

53
00:03:59,766 --> 00:04:01,128
that depend on it.

54
00:04:01,595 --> 00:04:06,657
Next, the Features button on the Tenants page opens the Features page of Bluebird.

55
00:04:06,657 --> 00:04:11,145
The same search finds nothing, so this tenant cannot enable any of them.

56
00:04:11,612 --> 00:04:20,213
Searching for OrchardCore.Email lists Email and SMTP Email Provider, but not Azure Communication Services Email.

57
00:04:20,213 --> 00:04:25,462
The wildcard rule excluded it, and the Include rule restored SMTP.

58
00:04:25,917 --> 00:04:30,647
Maplewood has no profile, so its Features page still lists Workflows.

59
00:04:30,647 --> 00:04:34,367
A profile only affects the tenants it is assigned to.

60
00:04:36,367 --> 00:04:39,167
A feature profile limits what a tenant is offered.

61
00:04:39,167 --> 00:04:42,617
Create it on the Default tenant, assign it to a tenant, and the

62
00:04:42,617 --> 00:04:45,267
Features page of that tenant follows its rules.

63
00:04:45,267 --> 00:04:46,567
Thanks for watching.

